<h3 data-start="331" data-end="375" class=""><strong data-start="335" data-end="375">1. Core Philosophy of Representation</strong></h3>
<div class="_tableContainer_16hzy_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="_tableWrapper_16hzy_14 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="377" data-end="1236" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="377" data-end="431"><tr data-start="377" data-end="431"><th data-start="377" data-end="386" data-col-size="sm">Aspect</th><th data-start="386" data-end="407" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="388" data-end="406">FER Hypothesis</strong></th><th data-start="407" data-end="431" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="409" data-end="429">TARTAN Framework</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="490" data-end="1236"><tr data-start="490" data-end="655"><td data-start="490" data-end="516" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="492" data-end="515">Representation View</strong></td><td data-start="516" data-end="580" data-col-size="lg">Emergent, unstructured, and entangled unless actively managed</td><td data-start="580" data-end="655" data-col-size="lg">Engineered, structured, semantically annotated, and physically grounded</td></tr><tr data-start="656" data-end="972"><td data-start="656" data-end="681" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="658" data-end="680">Problem Identified</strong></td><td data-start="681" data-end="812" data-col-size="lg">Representations become fractured (duplicated, scattered) and entangled (cross-dependent), reducing generalization and modularity</td><td data-start="812" data-end="972" data-col-size="lg">Current models lack <em data-start="834" data-end="863">semantic-physical anchoring</em>, failing to embed trajectories, forces, and intentions directly into pixel-space or latent representations</td></tr><tr data-start="973" data-end="1236"><td data-start="973" data-end="991" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="975" data-end="990">Ideal State</strong></td><td data-start="991" data-end="1092" data-col-size="lg">Unified and Factored Representations (UFRs): single mechanisms per concept, modular and composable</td><td 