<hr data-start="305" data-end="308" class="">
<h3 data-start="310" data-end="370" class=""><strong data-start="314" data-end="370">Comparative Analysis: TARTAN vs. Existing Frameworks</strong></h3>
<div class="_tableContainer_16hzy_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="_tableWrapper_16hzy_14 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="372" data-end="3448" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="372" data-end="550"><tr data-start="372" data-end="550"><th data-start="372" data-end="396" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="374" data-end="387">Framework</strong></th><th data-start="396" data-end="417" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="398" data-end="416">Core Principle</strong></th><th data-start="417" data-end="447" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="419" data-end="446">Semantic Representation</strong></th><th data-start="447" data-end="473" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="449" data-end="472">Physical Embodiment</strong></th><th data-start="473" data-end="496" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="475" data-end="495">Compositionality</strong></th><th data-start="496" data-end="520" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="498" data-end="519">Temporal Dynamics</strong></th><th data-start="520" data-end="550" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="522" data-end="548">Epistemic Auditability</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="735" data-end="3448"><tr data-start="735" data-end="1251"><td data-start="735" data-end="759" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="737" data-end="747">TARTAN</strong></td><td data-start="759" data-end="836" data-col-size="md">Category-theoretic layering of semantic, physical, and recursive structure</td><td data-start="836" data-end="944" data-col-size="lg">Fibered color-vector functor over object category; distinguishes symbolic identity, style, and ergodicity</td><td data-start="944" data-end="1019" data-col-size="md">Gaussian aura fields with velocity/temperature/density as sheaf sections</td><td data-start="1019" data-end="1089" data-col-size="md">Recursive tiling functor with natural transformations across layers</td><td data-start="1089" data-end="1165" data-col-size="md">Trajectory-aware pixel-stretching; motion encoded directly in image space</td><td data-start="1165" data-end="1251" data-col-size="md">Layered evidence bundles; steganographic overlays embed provenance and uncertainty</td></tr><tr data-start="1252" data-end="1750"><td data-start="1252" data-end="1276" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1254" data-end="1276">NeRF / Instant-NGP</strong></td><td data-start="1276" data-end="1332" data-col-size="md">Neural field interpolation using volumetric rendering</td><td data-start="1332" data-end="1430" data-col-size="lg">Implicit; scene categories not explicitly separated or differentiable without external labeling</td><td data-start="1430" data-end="1509" data-col-size="md">Density and color fields optimized for view synthesis, not physical fidelity</td><td data-start="1509" data-end="1587" data-col-size="md">Weak: Compositionality emerges from interpolation, not structured hierarchy</td><td data-start="1587" data-end="1662" data-col-size="md">Temporal NeRFs exist but are separately trained or require motion priors</td><td data-start="1662" data-end="1750" data-col-size="md">Low; interpolated representations with weak linkage to physical sensors or semantics</td></tr><tr data-start="1751" data-end="2183"><td data-start="1751" data-end="1775" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1753" data-end="1771">FER Hypothesis</strong></td><td data-start="1775" data-end="1842" data-col-size="md">Emergent function via embedding redundancy in transformer layers</td><td data-start="1842" data-end="1910" data-col-size="lg">Dense latent coactivation; semantics arise from statistical reuse</td><td data-start="1910" data-end="1977" data-col-size="md">Abstract; no commitment to physical realism or spatial grounding</td><td data-start="1977" data-end="2042" data-col-size="md">No modularity; everything is emergent from massive correlation</td><td data-start="2042" data-end="2112" data-col-size="md">Transformer-attended token history; lacks embodied motion coherence</td><td data-start="2112" data-end="2183" data-col-size="md">Opaque; redundancy is not labeled or recoverable to specific causes</td></tr><tr data-start="2184" data-end="2611"><td data-start="2184" data-end="2215" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2186" data-end="2214">ViT (Vision Transformer)</strong></td><td data-start="2215" data-end="2261" data-col-size="md">Self-attention over tokenized image patches</td><td data-start="2261" data-end="2335" data-col-size="lg">Emergent categories via attention heads; symbolic only after finetuning</td><td data-start="2335" data-end="2381" data-col-size="md">None; lacks physical properties or dynamics</td><td data-start="2381" data-end="2447" data-col-size="md">Weak modularity; compositionality is learned, not architectural</td><td data-start="2447" data-end="2527" data-col-size="md">Temporal handling requires extension (e.g., TimeSformer); motion not inherent</td><td data-start="2527" data-end="2611" data-col-size="md">Low; attention patterns are interpretable post hoc but not semantically grounded</td></tr><tr data-start="2612" data-end="3026"><td data-start="2612" data-end="2636" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2614" data-end="2630">Perceiver IO</strong></td><td data-start="2636" data-end="2672" data-col-size="md">Modality-agnostic attention model</td><td data-start="2672" data-end="2753" data-col-size="lg">Unified latent space, but semantically flat unless trained with aligned labels</td><td data-start="2753" data-end="2802" data-col-size="md">Possible with structured input, but not native</td><td data-start="2802" data-end="2878" data-col-size="md">Stronger: IO-query allows compositional prediction over structured inputs</td><td data-start="2878" data-end="2948" data-col-size="md">Encodes temporal patterns via attention; not kinematically embodied</td><td data-start="2948" data-end="3026" data-col-size="md">Medium; can be structured with labeled queries but lacks evidence layering</td></tr><tr data-start="3027" data-end="3448"><td data-start="3027" data-end="3071" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="3029" data-end="3070">Active Inference / Free Energy Models</strong></td><td data-start="3071" data-end="3126" data-col-size="md">Variational minimization of sensory prediction error</td><td data-start="3126" data-end="3186" data-col-size="lg">Emergent; tied to agent affordances and generative models</td><td data-start="3186" data-end="3252" data-col-size="md">Strong; body-based and predictive through sensorimotor coupling</td><td data-start="3252" data-end="3313" data-col-size="md">High, but implicitly defined by generative model structure</td><td data-start="3313" data-end="3377" data-col-size="md">Temporal dynamics modeled via state estimation and prediction</td><td data-start="3377" data-end="3448" data-col-size="md">High in theory, but implementations are sparse and non-standardized</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky end-(--thread-content-margin) h-0 self-end select-none"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end" style="height: 48.7031px;"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button class="bg-token-bg-primary hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-md-heavy"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M7 5C7 3.34315 8.34315 2 10 2H19C20.6569 2 22 3.34315 22 5V14C22 15.6569 20.6569 17 19 17H17V19C17 20.6569 15.6569 22 14 22H5C3.34315 22 2 20.6569 2 19V10C2 8.34315 3.34315 7 5 7H7V5ZM9 7H14C15.6569 7 17 8.34315 17 10V15H19C19.5523 15 20 14.5523 20 14V5C20 4.44772 19.5523 4 19 4H10C9.44772 4 9 4.44772 9 5V7ZM5 9C4.44772 9 4 9.44772 4 10V19C4 19.5523 4.44772 20 5 20H14C14.5523 20 15 19.5523 15 19V10C15 9.44772 14.5523 9 14 9H5Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></button></span></div></div></div></div>
