ned embeddings in latent language space</td><td data-start="1089" data-end="1143" data-col-size="md">Learned through reinforcement or imitation learning</td><td data-start="1143" data-end="1199" data-col-size="md">Manually defined ontologies or graph-structured data</td></tr><tr data-start="1200" data-end="1447"><td data-start="1200" data-end="1223" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1202" data-end="1222">Physics Modeling</strong></td><td data-start="1223" data-end="1302" data-col-size="md">Sheaf of aura fields over 4D spacetime manifold with thermodynamic grounding</td><td data-start="1302" data-end="1345" data-col-size="md">Implicit via latent statistical patterns</td><td data-start="1345" data-end="1391" data-col-size="md">Explicit simulation (e.g., Mujoco, Habitat)</td><td data-start="1391" data-end="1447" data-col-size="md">Hybrid; physics simulators paired with logical rules</td></tr><tr data-start="1448" data-end="1684"><td data-start="1448" data-end="1481" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1450" data-end="1480">Multi-Resolution Coherence</strong></td><td data-start="1481" data-end="1542" data-col-size="md">Recursive tiling and steganographic metadata across scales</td><td data-start="1542" data-end="1583" data-col-size="md">Single-scale attention-based smoothing</td><td data-start="1583" data-end="1629" data-col-size="md">Hierarchical world models (some multiscale)</td><td data-start="1629" data-end="1684" data-col-size="md">Weak or fragmented across symbolic/neural interface</td></tr><tr data-start="1685" data-end="1954"><td data-start="1685" data-end="1706" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1687" data-end="1705">Generalization</strong></td><td data-start="1706" data-end="1786" data-col-size="md">Constrained by physical and semantic priors; supports compositional recursion</td><td data-start="1786" data-end="1846" data-col-size="md">Large data-driven generalization; prone to hallucinations</td><td data-start="1846" data-end="1900" data-col-size="md">Grounded generalization but narrow domain expertise</td><td data-start="1900" data-end="1954" data-col-size="md">Moderate generalization through mixed architecture</td></tr><tr data-start="1955" data-end="2193"><td data-start="1955" data-end="1978" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1957" data-end="1977">Interpretability</strong></td><td data-start="1978" data-end="2052" data-col-size="md">Pre-hoc symbolic and physical annotations; explicit functorial mappings</td><td data-start="2052" data-end="2092" data-col-size="md">Post-hoc probing and saliency mapping</td><td data-start="2092" data-end="2141" data-col-size="md">Partially interpretable via environment states</td><td data-start="2141" data-end="2193" data-col-size="md">Transparent logic layers; opaque learned modules</td></tr><tr data-start="2194" data-end="2437"><td data-start="2194" data-end="2228" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2196" data-end="2227">Symbol-Physical Integration</strong></td><td data-start="2228" data-end="2291" data-col-size="md">Via natural transformations linking semantic and aura fields</td><td data-start="2291" data-end="2351" data-col-size="md">Lacks explicit integration; semantic symbols are emergent</td><td data-start="2351" data-end="2394" data-col-size="md">Tied to low-level sensor-action mappings</td><td data-start="2394" data-end="2437" data-col-size="md">Explicit but brittle integration points</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky end-(--thread-content-margin) h-0 self-end select-none"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end" style="height: 80.7031px;"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button class="bg-token-bg-primary hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-md-heavy"><path fill-rule="eve