<h2 data-start="2444" data-end="2486" class=""><strong data-start="2447" data-end="2486">Distinctive Contributions of TARTAN</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start="2488" data-end="2526" class="">1. <strong data-start="2495" data-end="2524">Mathematical Transparency</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2527" data-end="2744" class="">Unlike transformer-based models that rely on emergent representations from scale, TARTAN uses <em data-start="2621" data-end="2642">functorial mappings</em> and <em data-start="2647" data-end="2676">sheaf-theoretic constraints</em> to guarantee consistency and traceability of meaning across layers.</p>
<h3 data-start="2746" data-end="2777" class="">2. <strong data-start="2753" data-end="2775">Embodied Semantics</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2778" data-end="2974" class="">Whereas most embodied AI systems treat physics as an external simulation, TARTAN encodes physical parameters directly into aura fields, making physicality first-class in perception and generation.</p>
<h3 data-start="2976" data-end="3015" class="">3. <strong data-start="2983" data-end="3013">Recursive Compositionality</strong></h3>
<p data-start="3016" data-end="3280" class="">Compared to traditional multi-scale systems, TARTAN formalizes scale recursion via a <strong data-start="3101" data-end="3128">tower of tiling domains</strong> with steganographic integrity, enabling lossless recomposition from partial views‚Äîa capability lacking in current FER and scene reconstruction systems.</p>
<h3 data-start="3282" data-end="3341" class="">4. <strong data-start="3289" data-end="3339">Natural Transformations as Alignment Mechanism</strong></h3>
<p data-start="3342" data-end="3570" class="">TARTAN aligns symbolic, physical, and holographic layers via <strong data-start="3403" data-end="3430">natural transformations</strong>, a formal structure that supersedes the common "multi-modal fusion" in existing systems by enabling compositional reasoning between layers.</p>
