<p data-start="1650" data-end="1870" class="">TARTAN treats compression not as a lossy minimization problem but as a <strong data-start="1721" data-end="1744">semantic projection</strong>: a reduction in dimensionality <strong data-start="1776" data-end="1815">only along aligned categorical axes</strong>, maintaining coherence across time, space, and symbol.</p>
<hr data-start="1872" data-end="1875" class="">
<h3 data-start="1877" data-end="1950" class="">5. <strong data-start="1884" data-end="1950">Philosophical Divergence: Entropic Drift vs Negentropic Tiling</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1952" data-end="2126" class="">FER reflects the <strong data-start="1969" data-end="1987">entropic drift</strong> of neural representations under scale‚Äîwhere optimization amplifies incidental correlations, eventually forming high-dimensional spaghetti.</p>
<p data-start="2128" data-end="2417" class="">TARTAN resists this through <strong data-start="2156" data-end="2178">negentropic tiling</strong>: a commitment to structured compression via symmetries, embeddings, and physical laws. Its logic echoes the RSVP model of time‚Äîtreating representation as a trace of embodied geometry rather than an abstraction floating free of its source.</p>
<hr data-start="2419" data-end="2422" class="">
<h3 data-start="2424" data-end="2480" class="">6. <strong data-start="2431" data-end="2480">Toward a Unified Diagnostic‚ÄìPrescriptive Loop</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2482" data-end="2554" class="">A synthesis of FER and TARTAN could serve as a <strong data-start="2529" data-end="2553">closed feedback loop</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="2556" data-end="3015">
<li data-start="2556" data-end="2655" class="">
<p data-start="2558" data-end="2655" class=""><strong data-start="2558" data-end="2571">Diagnosis</strong>: Use FER tools to locate fractured and entangled subnetworks in large-scale models.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2656" data-end="2812" class="">
<p data-start="2658" data-end="2812" class=""><strong data-start="2658" data-end="2681">Prescriptive Repair</strong>: Apply TARTAN-inspired aura fields and tiling maps to <strong data-start="2736" data-end="2749">re-factor</strong> such regions into modular, physically interpretable subspaces.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2813" data-end="3015" class="">
<p data-start="2815" data-end="3015" class=""><strong data-start="2815" data-end="2843">Evolutionary Compression</strong>: Allow FER's open-ended evolution to explore configurations, but constrain it using <strong data-start="2928" data-end="2959">TARTAN‚Äôs categorical priors</strong> (e.g., semantic-physical alignment, tiling invariants).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3017" data-end="3237" class="">This loop offers a <strong data-start="3036" data-end="3059">hybrid epistemology</strong>: diagnosis through empirical probing, structure through mathematical embedding‚Äîa possible resolution to the tension between <strong data-start="3184" data-end="3206">post hoc emergence</strong> and <strong data-start="3211" data-end="3236">a priori architecture</strong>.</p>
