### What is RSVP Theory?

The Relativistic Scalar Vector Plenum (RSVP) theory is a cosmological model that rejects the idea of an expanding universe. Instead, it posits a static, structured plenum‚Äîa continuous field encoding scalar (density, potential) and vector (directional flow) properties‚Äîthat underlies all physical phenomena. Redshift, cosmic structure, and gravity aren‚Äôt driven by space stretching like some cosmic yoga class but by observer-dependent metric evolution within this plenum. Gravity emerges as entropic redistribution, and the universe‚Äôs evolution is a recursive dance of matter and vacuum dynamics.

RSVP integrates Mark Whittle‚Äôs (2008) vacuum pressure dynamics (‚Äúspace falling outward‚Äù during inflation) and Neil Turok‚Äôs (2016) entropic scale shift (expansion as loosening constraints), framing the cosmos as a thermodynamic process rather than a geometric balloon. It‚Äôs a bold middle finger to ŒõCDM‚Äôs reliance on dark energy and quantum fluctuations, addressing anomalies like the Hubble tension (~4.4œÉ; Riess et al., 2022) and CMB irregularities (Cold Spot, Axis of Evil) with a non-expanding, relational framework.

