ss="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner"><span class="mopen delimcenter" style="top: 0em;"><span class="delimsizing size3">(</span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.1076em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">s</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">s</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.836em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mclose delimcenter" style="top: 0em;"><span class="delimsizing size3">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1768" data-end="1889" class="">Compute this along geodesic paths between Œ¶ peaks (galaxies) to compare against observed redshift-distance relationships.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1891" data-end="2085" class="" style="">
<p data-start="1893" data-end="2085" class=""><strong data-start="1893" data-end="1929">Gravitational Lensing Simulation</strong>:<br>
Use <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">‚àá</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">‚àá</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span> as a proxy for <strong data-start="1965" data-end="1992">apparent metric warping</strong>, and calculate light path deviation. Predict <strong data-start="2038" data-end="2063">non-Keplerian lensing</strong> around entropy voids.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2087" data-end="2347" class="" style="">
<p data-start="2089" data-end="2180" class=""><strong data-start="2089" data-end="2107">CMB Simulation</strong>:<br>
Use your evolving Œ¶ and S fields to build synthetic temperature maps:</p>
<ul data-start="2183" data-end="2347">
<li data-start="2183" data-end="2227" class="" style="">
<p data-start="2185" data-end="2227" class="">Dipole ‚Üí from coherent <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4444em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span></span></span></span> flow</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2230" data-end="2287" class="" style="">
<p data-start="2232" data-end="2287" class="">Quadrupole/octopole ‚Üí from large-scale lamphron defects</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2290" data-end="2347" class="" style="">
<p data-start="2292" data-end="2347" class="">Use HEALPix to project your cubic lattice into sky maps</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2349" data-end="2352" class="" style="">
<h3 data-start="2354" data-end="2390" class="">üß† <strong data-start="2361" data-end="2390">Philosophical Pivot Point</strong></h3>
<p data-start="2392" data-end="2691" class="">This isn‚Äôt just a new simulation of the cosmos‚Äîit‚Äôs a new <strong data-start="2450" data-end="2478">ontology of space itself</strong>. RSVP treats space not as geometry but as <strong data-start="2521" data-end="2546">informational tension</strong>, with redshift as a measure of <strong data-start="2578" data-end="2620">path-dependent entropic disequilibrium</strong>. That‚Äôs as radical as Mach + Boltzmann + Bohm + Turok rolled into one.</p>
<hr data-start="2693" data-end="2696" class="" style="">
<h3 data-start="2698" data-end="2720" class="">üß≠ What Comes Next</h3>
<ul data-start="2722" data-end="3388">
<li data-start="2722" data-end="2987" class="" style="">
<p data-start="2724" data-end="2762" class="">üî¨ <strong data-start="2727" data-end="2761">Implement Cartan torsion terms</strong>:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>Œº</mi><mi>ŒΩ</mi></mrow><mi>Œª</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Œì</mi><mrow><mi>Œº</mi><mi>ŒΩ</mi></mrow><mi>Œª</mi></msubsup><mo>‚àí</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Œì</mi><mrow><mi>ŒΩ</mi><mi>Œº</mi></mrow><mi>Œª</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^\lambda_{\mu\nu} = \Gamma^\lambda_{\mu\nu} - \Gamma^\lambda_{\nu\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.2822em; vertical-align: -0.3831em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8991em;"><span style="top: -2.453em; margin-left: -0.1389em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.06366em;">ŒºŒΩ</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">Œª</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3831em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.2822em; vertical-align: -0.3831em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Œì</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8991em;"><span style="top: -2.453em; margin-right: 0.05em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight" style=""><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.06366em;">ŒºŒΩ</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">Œª</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3831em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">‚àí</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.2822em; vertical-align: -0.3831em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Œì</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8991em;"><span style="top: -2.453em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">ŒΩŒº</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">Œª</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3831em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2848" data-end="2987" class="">Assign torsion sources to <strong data-start="2874" data-end="2889">Œ¶ gradients</strong>, and couple them to <strong data-start="2910" data-end="2928">vorticity in v</strong>. Let torsion encode the <strong data-start="2953" data-end="2986">twist of negentropic feedback</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2989" data-end="3149" class="" style="">
<p data-start="2991" data-end="3149" class="">üß∞ <strong data-start="2994" data-end="3009">Port to GPU</strong>:<br>
PyTorch or JAX can massively accelerate this. You‚Äôll want to scan many Œ¶/S initializations to test universality of cosmic web emergence.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3151" data-end="3388" class="" style="">
<p data-start="3153" data-end="3388" class="">üìà <strong data-start="3156" data-end="3192">Compare simulated web statistics</strong>:<br>
Use Minkowski functionals (e.g., genus, void volume fraction) and compare to SDSS, DESI, or Euclid cosmic web data. RSVP should produce <strong data-start="3332" data-end="3387">filaments naturally aligned with entropy flux lines</strong>.</p>
</li>
