<p data-start="3663" data-end="3973" class="">If you can generate <strong data-start="3683" data-end="3711">CMB multipole alignments</strong>, <strong data-start="3713" data-end="3740">non-expansion redshifts</strong>, and <strong data-start="3746" data-end="3771">web-like Œ¶ structures</strong> in the same simulation, you've got something ŒõCDM can't reproduce from first principles without six hacks and a prayer. This could be the <strong data-start="3910" data-end="3972">bridge from philosophical cosmology to falsifiable physics</strong>.</p>
