<hr data-start="316" data-end="319" class="" style="">
<h3 data-start="321" data-end="425" class=""><strong data-start="325" data-end="425">The Fall of Space: Entropic Relaxation and Structure Without Expansion in a Scalar-Vector Plenum</strong></h3>
<h4 data-start="427" data-end="444" class=""><strong data-start="432" data-end="444">Abstract</strong></h4>
<p data-start="446" data-end="1139" class="">We present a lattice-based simulation framework for modeling a non-expanding cosmological medium described by the Relativistic Scalar Vector Plenum (RSVP) theory. This framework reinterprets gravitation and cosmic evolution through the interplay of a scalar density field <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Œ¶</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Œ¶</span></span></span></span>, a dynamic vector field <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>‚Éó</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.714em;"></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.714em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="accent-body" style="left: -0.2077em;"><span class="overlay" style="height: 0.714em; width: 0.471em;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="0.471em" height="0.714em" viewBox="0 0 471 714" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin" style="width: 0.471em;"><path d="M377 20c0-5.333 1.833-10 5.5-14S391 0 397 0c4.667 0 8.667 1.667 12 5
