<h3 data-start="6689" data-end="6707" class=""><strong data-start="6693" data-end="6707">Conclusion</strong></h3>
<p data-start="6709" data-end="7185" class="">The RSVP lattice simulation demonstrates that structured evolution of a scalar-vector-entropy plenum can reproduce key cosmological phenomena without assuming metric expansion or dark components. By reframing gravity as entropic smoothing and structure as a negentropic attractor, this model reimagines the cosmos as a recursively computable system. As a framework, it invites further exploration of physics at the intersection of information, entropy, and emergent causality.</p>
