We formalize the **Relativistic Scalar Vector Plenum (RSVP)** cosmological framework through a lattice field theory where redshift, cosmic structure, and gravitational effects emerge from the recursive interaction of a scalar density field (Œ¶), a vector flow field (**v**), and an entropy gradient (S). Unlike ŒõCDM‚Äôs expanding spacetime, RSVP treats the universe as a **static but dynamically reorganizing plenum**, with "space falling outward" via entropic redistribution rather than metric expansion. Using discrete 3D lattice simulations, we demonstrate how:&nbsp;&nbsp;
