>
<hr data-start="112" data-end="115" class="" style="">
<h3 data-start="117" data-end="206" class="">Academic Summary: The Relativistic Scalar Vector Plenum (RSVP) Cosmological Framework</h3>
<p data-start="208" data-end="844" class="">The <strong data-start="212" data-end="256">Relativistic Scalar Vector Plenum (RSVP)</strong> theory offers a radical alternative to the standard ŒõCDM cosmological model by rejecting metric expansion of spacetime in favor of a <strong data-start="390" data-end="443">static but dynamically reorganizing cosmic plenum</strong>. This plenum is modeled as a coupled system of three fundamental fields: a scalar density field (Œ¶), a negentropic vector flow field (<strong data-start="578" data-end="583">v</strong>), and an entropy gradient field (S). Together, these form a nonlinear scalar-vector-entropy (SVE) triad that governs cosmic structure, gravitational phenomena, and redshift effects through entropic and dynamic interactions rather than expansion or dark matter.</p>
<p data-start="846" data-end="885" class=""><strong data-start="846" data-end="885">Core contributions of RSVP include:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="887" data-end="2765">
<li data-start="887" data-end="1278" class="" style="">
<p data-start="889" data-end="1278" class=""><strong data-start="889" data-end="921">Entropic Redshift Mechanism:</strong> Instead of Doppler shifts from recessional velocities, redshift emerges as a line-of-sight integral of entropy gradients (z ‚àù ‚à´‚àáS¬∑dx), providing a natural explanation for the observed Hubble law without requiring universal expansion. This framework can also address observed anomalies at high redshift, suggesting testable deviations from ŒõCDM predictions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1280" data-end="1705" class="" style="">
<p data-start="1282" data-end="1705" class=""><strong data-start="1282" data-end="1340">Cosmic Web Formation Without Inflation or Dark Matter:</strong> Lattice simulations of the Œ¶‚Äì<strong data-start="1370" data-end="1375">v</strong>‚ÄìS system reveal spontaneous formation of filamentary structures and voids driven by entropic constraint relaxation and flow dynamics, obviating the need for inflationary initial conditions or particle dark matter halos. The <strong data-start="1600" data-end="1621">‚Äúfalling outward‚Äù</strong> vector flows represent a novel physical intuition for how space itself reorganizes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1707" data-end="2079" class="" style="">
<p data-start="1709" data-end="2079" class=""><strong data-start="1709" data-end="1746">Resolution of Key ŒõCDM Anomalies:</strong> RSVP offers plausible explanations for the <strong data-start="1790" data-end="1808">Hubble tension</strong> through anisotropic entropic gradients, models CMB anomalies such as the Axis of Evil via plenum shear fields, and predicts void lensing effects from vector field vorticity rather than dark energy. Quantized redshift phenomena arise naturally from plenum harmonic modes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2081" data-end="2383" class="" style="">
<p data-start="2083" data-end="2383" class=""><strong data-start="2083" data-end="2111">Mathematical Extensions:</strong> Incorporation of <strong data-start="2129" data-end="2147">Cartan torsion</strong> as a geometric representation of plenomic vorticity extends the model into non-Riemannian cosmology, linking to modified gravity frameworks and providing a geometric basis for emergent MOND-like dynamics without invoking exotic matter.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2385" data-end="2765" class="" style="">
<p data-start="2387" data-end="2765" class=""><strong data-start="2387" data-end="2436">Philosophical and Computational Implications:</strong> RSVP conceptualizes the universe as a <strong data-start="2475" data-end="2509">computationally ergodic system</strong>, continuously recomputing its structure through recursive scalar-vector-entropy feedback loops. Observers are understood as viviceptive processes embedded within this plenum, aligning with relational and informational interpretations of quantum mechanics.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2767" data-end="3159" class=""><strong data-start="2767" data-end="2801">Future Directions and Roadmap:</strong> A four-phase program is proposed, starting with formal mathematical grounding and small-scale simulations, followed by observational testing against datasets from DESI, Euclid, and JWST, scaling up to high-resolution lattice runs incorporating torsion effects, and culminating in the consolidation of RSVP as a predictive, falsifiable cosmological paradigm.</p>
<hr data-start="3161" data-end="3164" class="" style="">
<p data-start="3166" data-end="3495" class="">In summary, RSVP challenges conventional cosmology by replacing spacetime expansion and dark components with an entropically driven, scalar-vector plenum. Its predictive successes and conceptual coherence position it as a compelling framework for rethinking the cosmos, warranting further theoretical and empirical investigation.</p>
<hr data-start="3497" data-end="3500" class="">
